    {
      "text": "canst thou read this without rejoicing, D&C 19:39. lift up thy heart and rejoice, D&C 25:13. gospel to be declared with sound of rejoicing, D&C 28:16 (29:4). Zion shall rejoice upon hills, D&C 35:24 (49:25). he who preaches and he who receives are both edified and rejoice together, D&C 50:22. warning against being overcome, neither with boasting nor rejoicing, D&C 50:33. let him who receives of God rejoice that he is accounted worthy to receive, D&C 50:34. fasting and prayer, or in other words, rejoicing and prayer, D&C 59:14. angels rejoice over elders who have borne testimony, D&C 62:3. he who does not receive gift rejoices not in that gift, nor rejoices in giver, D&C 88:33. let Zion rejoice, D&C 97:21. your sins are forgiven, lift up your heads and rejoice, D&C 110:5. the Lord will make handmaid’s heart to rejoice, D&C 132:56. the Lord will meet him who rejoices and works righteousness, D&C 133:44. spirits of just rejoice in their redemption, D&C 138:15, 18, 23.",
